# [[.Name]]

Go queue consumer. Generated by kickhub from `[[.Template]]` v[[.Version]], target **[[.Target]]**.

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `cmd/worker` | Entry point and `handle`, where your logic goes |
| `internal/queue/queue.go` | Queue interface the worker depends on |
| `internal/queue/provider.go` | The only target-specific code: the broker adapter |
[[ if eq .Target "local" -]]
| `docker-compose.yml` | ElasticMQ, queue bootstrap and the worker |
[[- else -]]
| `infra/` | Terraform for the queue, dead-letter queue and consumer identity |
[[- end ]]
| `.kickhub.yaml` | Records the template, version and parameters used |

## Run it
[[ if eq .Target "local" ]]
```sh
make up              # starts ElasticMQ, creates the queue, starts the worker
make send MSG=hello  # publishes one message
make logs            # watch the worker process it
make down
```
[[ else if eq .Target "aws" ]]
```sh
make test
make infra-apply
QUEUE_URL="$(terraform -chdir=infra output -raw queue_url)" AWS_REGION=[[.P.aws_region]] go run ./cmd/worker
```

A message that fails [[.P.max_deliveries]] times moves to the dead-letter queue. Attach the `consumer_policy_arn` output to the role that runs the worker.
[[ else ]]
```sh
make test
make infra-apply
GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=[[.P.gcp_project]] SUBSCRIPTION="$(terraform -chdir=infra output -raw subscription)" go run ./cmd/worker
```

A message that fails [[.P.max_deliveries]] times moves to the dead-letter topic. Run the worker as the `worker_service_account` output.
[[ end ]]
## Before production

- This repo provisions the messaging resources, not the compute. Deploy the image from `Dockerfile` to your platform of choice.
- Keep `handle` idempotent: delivery is at-least-once.
- Move Terraform state to a remote backend and commit `go.sum`.
